lease.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_release.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_relaxed.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_relaxed.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_relaxed.alt_3"],"text":"Boolean natural-width compare-exchange is offered in full, acquire, release and relaxed orderings. It reports success and on failure refreshes the caller-provided expected value with the currently observed contents. Absent a dedicated architecture boolean form, it is expressed through the raw value-returning compare-exchange of matching ordering."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_acquire.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_acquire.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_acquire.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_acquire.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_release.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_release.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_release.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_release.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_relaxed.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_relaxed.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_relaxed.alt_3"],"text":"Boolean 64-bit compare-exchange is offered in full, acquire, release and relaxed orderings with the same success-report plus expected-value refresh contract, falling back to the raw 64-bit value-returning compare-exchange of matching ordering when no dedicated architecture boolean form exists."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_acquire.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_acquire.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_acquire.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_acquire.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_release.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_release.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_release.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_release.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_relaxed.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_relaxed.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_relaxed.alt_3"],"text":"Boolean 128-bit compare-exchange is offered in full, acquire, release and relaxed orderings with the same success-report plus expected-value refresh contract, falling back to the raw 128-bit value-returning compare-exchange of matching ordering when no dedicated architecture boolean form exists."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_cmpxchg_local","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_local.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg_local.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_cmpxchg64_local","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_local.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg64_local.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_cmpxchg128_local","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_local.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_try_cmpxchg128_local.alt_2","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_sync_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_sync_try_cmpxchg.alt_1","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_sync_try_cmpxchg.alt_2"],"text":"Processor-local and synchronous compare-exchange families are exposed for natural, 64-bit and 128-bit widths, each with value-returning and boolean forms. Value forms delegate directly to the corresponding architecture local or synchronous primitive, and boolean forms use a dedicated architecture boolean primitive where present or the matching local or synchronous value form otherwise."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_set_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_acquire"],"text":"Raw atomic integer accessors cover ordered load-acquire, plain store, ordered store-release, unordered add, and add-return plus fetch-add in full, acquire, release and relaxed orderings. Each prefers its dedicated architecture variant and otherwise synthesizes the requested ordering from the relaxed architecture variant plus fences or reuses the fully ordered architecture variant."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/atomic.h::atomic_cond_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_set_release"],"text":"An atomic integer object exposes a directly addressable integer member holding its value. Ordered and conditional accesses operate on that member rather than through an opaque accessor."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_set_release"],"text":"Ordered atomic load and store select their mechanism by whether the atomic representation occupies a native machine word. Native-word cases use a single ordered access, while other cases combine a plain access with the corresponding acquire or release fence. Architecture-specific ordered accessors take precedence when defined."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::_LINUX_ATOMIC_FALLBACK_H"],"text":"The architecture fallback header is protected by a multiple-inclusion guard macro defined once for the translation unit."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_xchg.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_xchg_acquire.alt_4","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_cmpxchg.alt_3","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_acquire"],"text":"Absent architecture support is a build-time failure rather than a silent fallback. Exchange and compare-exchange families resolve to not-implemented markers, and add-return and fetch-add families use an explicit compile error. Some relaxed or weaker-ordering requests may reuse the fully ordered architecture operation and therefore be stronger than requested."},{"kind"